          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesHadronsAsKKModesOf5dYangMillsTheory"} Hadrons as KK-modes of 5d Yang-Mills theory
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#history"} History
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The idea of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+theory"} Kaluza-Klein theory
            has traditionally been applied mostly to “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"}> color physics
            ”, such as in attempts to realize the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charges"} color charges
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+chromodynamics"} quantum chromodynamics
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gluons"} gluons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+supergravity"} heterotic supergravity
            (see for instance at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
                –
                %a{:href => "string+phenomenology#ReferencesHeteroticModels"} heterotic models
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/landscape+of+string+theory+vacua"} landscape of string theory vacua
          %p
            Alternatively, Kaluza-Klein theory may be considered for “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+physics"}> flavor physics
            ” to produce the charges of
            = succeed "-\u201C" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+physics"} flavor
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hidden+local+symmetries"} hidden local symmetries
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadrons"} hadrons
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+hadrodynamics"} quantum hadrodynamics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+QFT"} geometric engineering of QFT
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
            this means to consider
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            on
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+branes"} flavor branes
            (instead of on
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+branes"} color branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto+model"} Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto model
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color charge
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+physics"} flavor charge
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+bosons"} gauge bosons
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gluons"} gluons
                  %br/
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"}> gauge group
                  \-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+symmetry"}> local symmetry
                  )
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
                  %br/
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+physics"}> flavor
                  \-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hidden+local+symmetry"}> hidden local symmetry
                  )
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermions"} fermions
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
          %p
            Indeed, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experimentally
            observed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
            appear in towers of increasing mass (“higher resonances”), which may usefully be identified as a Kaluza-Klein tower of the single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+boson"} gauge boson
            of an
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%282%29"} SU(2)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=5 Yang-Mills theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#SonStephanov03"}> Son-Stephanov 03
            ).
          %p
            Moreover, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion+field"} pion field
            appears as the gauge 0-mode of this tower, right away in its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/soliton"} solitonic
            incarnation as the
            = succeed "-excitation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmion"} Skyrmion
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AtiyahManton89"} Atiyah-Manton 89
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Sutcliffe10"} Sutcliffe 10
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Sutcliffe15"} Sutcliffe 15
          %p
            Various qualitative phenomena of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenology
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+hadrodynamics"} quantum hadrodynamics
            find a natural explanation in hadron Kaluza-Klein theory this way, notably:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hidden+local+symmetry"} hidden local symmetry
                itself (by the very KK-reduction of a gauge theory)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson+dominance"} vector meson dominance
                (as discussed there)
            %li
              %p QCD sum rules (…)
            %li
              %p (…)
          %p
            In terms of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+brane"} flavor brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=5 Yang-Mills theory
            which gives
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+hadrodynamics"} quantum hadrodynamics
            this way naturally arises on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4%2FD8-brane+intersections"} D4/D8-brane intersections
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto+model"} Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto model
            (
            %a{:href => "#SakaiSugimoto04"}> Sakai-Sugimoto 04
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#SakaiSugimoto05"} Sakai-Sugimoto 05
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wrapped+brane"} wrapped
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+interval"} closed interval
            (
            %a{:href => "#IvanovaLechtenfeldPopov18"}> Ivanova-Lechtenfeld-Popov 18
            )
          %p
            Already to first approximation, this produces for instance
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon"} baryon
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            spectra with moderate quantitative agreement with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            (
            %a{:href => "#HSSY07"}> HSSY 07
            ):
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BaryonSpectrumInSakaiSugimoto.jpg", :width => "700"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#Sugimoto16"} Sugimoto 16
          %p
            An extensive review of hadron Kaluza-Klein theory may be found in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#RhoEtAl16"} Rho et al 16
          %p
            Strikingly, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experimentally
            observed
            = succeed "-spectrum" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron"} hadron
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron+supersymmetry"} hadron supersymmetry
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron+supersymmetry"} hadron supersymmetry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto+model"} Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto model
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+hadrodynamics"} quantum hadrodynamics
          %h2#references References
          %div
            %h3#ReferencesHadronsAsKKModesOf5dYangMillsTheory Hadrons as KK-modes of 5d Yang-Mills theory
            %p
              The suggestion that the tower of observed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+mesons"} vector mesons
              – when regarded as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hidden+local+symmetry"} hidden local symmetries
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+perturbation+theory"} chiral perturbation theory
              – is reasonably modeled as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+theory"} Kaluza-Klein tower
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=5 Yang-Mills theory
            %ul
              %li#SonStephanov03
                D. T. Son, M. A. Stephanov,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em QCD and dimensional deconstruction
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0304182"} arXiv:hep-ph/0304182
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.69.065020"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.69.065020
            %p
              That the pure
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"} pion
              = succeed "-model" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmion"} Skyrmion
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
              is approximately the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+theory"} KK-reduction
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=5 Yang-Mills theory
              is already due to:
            %ul
              %li#AtiyahManton89
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+Manton"} Nicholas Manton
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Skyrmions from instantons
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(89)90340-7"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(89)90340-7
            %p
              with a
              = succeed "-variant" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+space"} hyperbolic space
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Sutcliffe"} Paul Sutcliffe
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Skyrmions, instantons, mass and curvature
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0411052"} arXiv:hep-th/0411052
            %p Further discussion of this approximation:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Josh+Cork"}> Josh Cork
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Halcrow"} Chris Halcrow
                %em ADHM skyrmions
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.15190"}> arXiv:2110.15190
                )
            %p
              The observation that the result of
              %a{:href => "#AtiyahManton89"} Atiyah-Manton 89
              becomes an exact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+theory"} Kaluza-Klein construction
              of
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmions"} Skyrmions
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
              from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=5
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
              when the full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+theory"} KK-tower
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+mesons"} vector mesons
              as in
              %a{:href => "#SonStephanov03"} Son-Stephanov 03
              is included into the Skyrmion model (see also
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "skyrmion#ReferencesSkyrmeHadrodynamicsWithVectorMesons"} there
            %ul
              %li#Sutcliffe10
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Sutcliffe"}> Paul Sutcliffe
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Skyrmions, instantons and holography
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1003.0023"} arXiv:1003.0023
              %li#Sutcliffe15
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Sutcliffe"}> Paul Sutcliffe
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Holographic Skyrmions
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/1383608"} spire:1383608
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217984915400515"} doi:10.1142/S0217984915400515
            %p
              In the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sakai-Sugimoto+model"} Sakai-Sugimoto model
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=5 Yang-Mills theory
              of this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron+Kaluza-Klein+theory"} hadron Kaluza-Klein theory
              is identified with the
              = succeed "-theory" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-brane"} D8
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+branes"} flavour branes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4%2FD8-brane+intersection"} intersected with D4-branes
              in an
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+model"} intersecting D-brane model
            %ul
              %li#SakaiSugimoto04
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadakatsu+Sakai"}> Tadakatsu Sakai
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shigeki+Sugimoto"} Shigeki Sugimoto
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Low energy hadron physics in holographic QCD
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0412141"} arXiv:hep-th/0412141
              %li#SakaiSugimoto05
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadakatsu+Sakai"}> Tadakatsu Sakai
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shigeki+Sugimoto"} Shigeki Sugimoto
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em More on a holographic dual of QCD
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0507073"} arXiv:hep-th/0507073
              %li#HSSY07
                %p
                  Hiroyuki Hata,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadakatsu+Sakai"} Tadakatsu Sakai
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shigeki+Sugimoto"} Shigeki Sugimoto
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Baryons from instantons in holographic QCD
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0701280"} arXiv:hep-th/0701280
              %li#BolognesiSutcliffe13
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefano+Bolognesi"}> Stefano Bolognesi
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Sutcliffe"} Paul Sutcliffe
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The Sakai-Sugimoto soliton
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.1396"} arXiv:1309.1396
              %li#Bartolini17
                %p
                  Lorenzo Bartolini,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefano+Bolognesi"} Stefano Bolognesi
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em From the Sakai-Sugimoto Model to the Generalized Skyrme Model
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.03873"} arXiv:1711.03873
            %p
              Extensive review of this
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic
              = succeed "-realization" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+theory"} KK-theoretic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+hadrodynamics"} quantum hadrodynamics
              from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=5 Yang-Mills theory
              is in:
            %ul
              %li#RhoEtAl16
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mannque+Rho"}> Mannque Rho
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ismail+Zahed"} Ismail Zahed
                  (eds.)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Multifaceted+Skyrmion"} The Multifaceted Skyrmion
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9710"} doi:10.1142/9710
                %ul
                  %li#Sugimoto16
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shigeki+Sugimoto"}> Shigeki Sugimoto
                    ,
                    = succeed "," do
                      %em Skyrmion and String theory
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mannque+Rho"} Mannque Rho
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ismail+Zahed"} Ismail Zahed
                    (eds.)
                    = succeed "," do
                      %em
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Multifaceted+Skyrmion"} The Multifaceted Skyrmion
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9710"} doi:10.1142/9710
            %p
              Via the realization of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4%2FD8+brane+bound+states"} D4/D8 brane bound states
              as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-brane"} D8-brane
              = succeed "-theory" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
              %a{:href => "DpDpPlus4BraneBoundState#AsYangMillsInstantons"} there
              and
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "D4-D8+brane+bound+state#AsInstantonsOnTheD8Brane"} there
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
              as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wrapped+brane"} wrapped
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-branes"} D4-branes
            %ul
              %li#Witten98b
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Baryons And Branes In Anti de Sitter Space
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9805112"} arXiv:hep-th/9805112
              %li#GrossOoguri98
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gross"}> David Gross
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hirosi+Ooguri"} Hirosi Ooguri
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      Aspects of Large
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi N
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
